# Data environment stabilization

Read `docs/DATA_ENVIRONMENT_STABILIZATION_PLAN.md` before changing database,
backup, Git, sync, deploy, environment, hook, or DreamHost behavior.

- Keep live auto-push disabled. Editor hooks must not target production.
- Keep `USE_PROD_DB=false` unless the owner explicitly authorizes the exact
  production operation in the current mission.
- Full data copies flow production → local/staging only. Never replace live
  operational data with a staging/local database.
- Production promotion moves a committed code artifact, schema migrations, and
  explicitly reviewed reference-data patches—not a whole staging dump.
- The nightly mirror and weekly backups are never test targets.
- Tests must target exactly the disposable production-derived test database.
- Git is additive during recovery: no reset, clean, force-push, history rewrite,
  checkout-overwrite, or broad staging.
- No database dumps, credentials, uploads, logs, or production PII enter Git.
- Stop at the owner gates listed in the plan. Record every phase in Homebase.

